{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 437173, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 20]], "date-time": "2026-05-20T15:10:54Z", "timestamp": 1779289854132, "version": "3.51.4"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "ASEE Conferences", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.18260/1-2--58486", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 20]], "date-time": "2026-05-20T14:16:40Z", "timestamp": 1779286600000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["WIP: Training Prompt Engineering Skills in AI-Assisted Programmatic Labeling Tasks"], "prefix": "10.18260", "author": [{"given": "Duy", "family": "Tran", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Delaware"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Qile", "family": "Wang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Delaware"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Matthew", "family": "Mauriello", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Delaware"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "7582", "event": {"name": "2026 Spring Middle Atlantic Section Conference", "location": "University of Delaware, Delaware", "start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 27]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 28]]}}, "container-title": ["2026 Spring Middle Atlantic Section Conference Proceedings"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 20]], "date-time": "2026-05-20T14:16:59Z", "timestamp": 1779286619000}, "score": 28.017475, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://peer.asee.org/58486"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.18260/1-2--58486"}, {"institution": [{"name": "ScienceOpen"}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 12]], "date-time": "2026-01-12T17:27:42Z", "timestamp": 1768238862622, "version": "3.49.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 19]]}, "reference-count": 1, "publisher": "ScienceOpen", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 19]], "date-time": "2025-12-19T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1766102400000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Agentic artificial intelligence (AI) represents a significant departure from traditional task-level automation by enabling autonomous, goal-directed systems capable of performing multi-step workflows. This research investigates how agentic AI reconfigures occupational structures across industries, shifting the analysis from discrete task substitution to the transformation of entire roles. Using a mixed-methods approach that integrates cross-industry case studies, role-content analysis, and qualitative insights from organizational leaders, the study identifies five dominant patterns of role transformation: consolidation, segmentation, elevation, displacement, and creation. Findings reveal that agentic AI not only reshapes job boundaries but also alters organizational hierarchies, workflow coordination, and skill requirements. The study offers a conceptual framework for understanding the transition from task-based to role-based redesign and provides strategic recommendations for policymakers, organizations, and workforce planners navigating the emerging agentic-economy landscape.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.14293/pr2199.002638.v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 12]], "date-time": "2026-01-12T14:05:13Z", "timestamp": 1768226713000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["From Tasks to Roles: How Agentic AI Reconfigures Occupational Structures Across Industries"], "prefix": "10.14293", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6878-9605", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "